  "title": "Chapter 46: Banking System in India",
  "order": 46,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z4zfp12",
      "content": "The banking system plays a crucial role in the economic development of a country. Banks mobilize savings from the public and provide loans for investment and development. The Indian banking system includes the Reserve Bank of India, commercial banks, regional rural banks and cooperative banks."
    },
    {
