    {
      "id": "on40tvy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Banking"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) is the central monetary authority responsible for regulating the Indian financial sector.",
        "Commercial banks in India are structured into Public Sector, Private Sector, Foreign Banks, and Regional Rural Banks (RRBs).",
        "RBI formulates and executes Monetary Policy using quantitative tools (CRR, SLR, Repo Rate) and qualitative tools to maintain price stability.",
        "Modern banking relies heavily on digital financial infrastructure including NEFT, RTGS, IMPS, and digital payment frameworks."
      ],
      "id": "d2gisrb"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2f3uze9",
      "content": "• Banking refers to the business of accepting deposits and providing loans."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "avh7fa8",
      "content": "• Banks act as financial intermediaries between savers and borrowers."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7iew5iv",
      "content": "• They facilitate economic development by promoting savings and investments."
    },
    {
